cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Vanargand: a partition-tolerant ledger design for intermittently connected networks"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Geri"
    given-names: "Freki"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-7503-459X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gerifreki99/vanargand"
abstract: >-
  Vanargand is a design for a distributed ledger in which network partition is the
  normal operating regime rather than a failure mode. It covers a finality
  ladder with deterministic reconciliation, bounded offline spending with
  self-proving account equivocation, and payment channels hardened against
  closure during partition.
keywords:
  - distributed ledger
  - partition tolerance
  - offline payments
  - payment channels
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - byzantine fault tolerance
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-18"
